= How to use this guide

This document explains how the current project works by following a source file from bytes on disk through tokens, syntax tree, evaluation, memory, trace capture, and rendering. It emphasizes the code that runs today, while calling out older or unfinished subsystems that can look like the active compiler at first glance.

The goal is not to read every line in one sitting. Use the route below, keep the repository open, and run the examples as you go. The times include reading the relevant code and pausing to inspect a couple of executions.

